---
import DocsLayout from "@/layouts/DocsLayout.astro";
import DocPageShell from "@/components/DocPageShell.astro";
import CodeBlock from "@/components/CodeBlock.astro";
---
<DocsLayout
	title="CLI — ayjnt docs"
	description="Every ayjnt command, its arguments, exit codes, and the flags that get forwarded to wrangler."
>
	<DocPageShell
		slug="reference/cli"
		lede="ayjnt ships one CLI with five subcommands. This is the per-command reference."
	>
		<h2>Invocation</h2>
		<p>
			Run via <code>bunx ayjnt &lt;subcommand&gt;</code> from any directory,
			or through a project <code>package.json</code> script (scaffolded by{" "}
			<code>ayjnt new</code>). The CLI operates on the current working
			directory by default; override with <code>--cwd &lt;path&gt;</code>.
		</p>

		<h3>Global flags</h3>
		<table>
			<thead>
				<tr>
					<th>Flag</th>
					<th>Meaning</th>
				</tr>
			</thead>
			<tbody>
				<tr>
					<td>
						<code>--cwd &lt;path&gt;</code>
					</td>
					<td>Project root (default: <code>process.cwd()</code>)</td>
				</tr>
				<tr>
					<td>
						<code>--force</code>
					</td>
					<td>
						Only meaningful for <code>deploy</code>. Skips git preflight.
					</td>
				</tr>
				<tr>
					<td>
						<code>-h, --help</code>
					</td>
					<td>Print usage.</td>
				</tr>
			</tbody>
		</table>
		<p>
			Any flag ayjnt doesn't recognize is passed through to{" "}
			<code>wrangler</code>. So{" "}
			<code>ayjnt dev --port 9000</code> forwards <code>--port 9000</code>{" "}
			to <code>wrangler dev</code>.
		</p>

		<h2>ayjnt new</h2>
		<CodeBlock lang="sh" code={`ayjnt new <directory> [--empty]`} />
		<p>
			Scaffolds a new ayjnt project at <code>&lt;directory&gt;</code>.
			Fails if the directory already exists.
		</p>
		<table>
			<thead>
				<tr>
					<th>Flag</th>
					<th>Effect</th>
				</tr>
			</thead>
			<tbody>
				<tr>
					<td>
						<code>--empty</code>
					</td>
					<td>
						Skip the UI — scaffold a single bare "I'm alive" agent and
						no React. Default includes a UI (home page + counter).
					</td>
				</tr>
			</tbody>
		</table>
		<h3>What gets created</h3>
		<CodeBlock
			lang="sh"
			code={`my-app/
├── agents/
│   └── chat/agent.ts       # --empty; default adds counter/ + agents/app.tsx
├── package.json            # with dev/build/deploy/migrate scripts
├── tsconfig.json           # path aliases pre-wired
├── .gitignore              # .ayjnt/* except migrations.json
└── README.md`}
		/>
		<h3>Exit codes</h3>
		<ul>
			<li><code>0</code> — scaffolded successfully.</li>
			<li>
				<code>1</code> — directory already exists, or argument validation
				failed.
			</li>
		</ul>

		<h2>ayjnt dev</h2>
		<CodeBlock lang="sh" code={`ayjnt dev [wrangler-flags...]`} />
		<p>
			Runs the codegen pipeline then spawns <code>wrangler dev</code>
			pointed at <code>.ayjnt/dist/wrangler.jsonc</code>. Watches{" "}
			<code>agents/</code> for structural changes and re-runs codegen on
			the fly.
		</p>
		<h3>What gets watched</h3>
		<p>
			Any file under <code>agents/</code> matching{" "}
			<code>**/agent.ts</code>, <code>**/middleware.ts</code>, or{" "}
			<code>**/app.tsx</code>. Structural changes — adding a new agent
			folder, renaming, deleting — trigger a 150ms-debounced rebuild.
		</p>
		<p>
			Wrangler itself picks up changes to the compiled worker and
			assets. Content-only edits (changing the body of an agent method)
			are reloaded by wrangler without ayjnt needing to do anything.
		</p>
		<h3>Forwarded wrangler flags</h3>
		<p>
			Common ones that just pass through:
		</p>
		<ul>
			<li><code>--port &lt;port&gt;</code> — default 8787</li>
			<li><code>--host &lt;host&gt;</code> — default localhost</li>
			<li><code>--ip &lt;ip&gt;</code> — bind to a specific interface</li>
			<li><code>--remote</code> — run the worker on Cloudflare infrastructure instead of locally</li>
		</ul>
		<h3>Exit codes</h3>
		<ul>
			<li><code>0</code> — wrangler exited cleanly.</li>
			<li>
				<em>wrangler's exit code</em> — propagated if wrangler fails.
			</li>
		</ul>

		<h2>ayjnt build</h2>
		<CodeBlock lang="sh" code={`ayjnt build`} />
		<p>
			Pure codegen, no deploy. Writes:
		</p>
		<ul>
			<li><code>.ayjnt/dist/entry.ts</code> (worker entrypoint)</li>
			<li><code>.ayjnt/dist/wrangler.jsonc</code></li>
			<li><code>.ayjnt/tsconfig.json</code> (path aliases)</li>
			<li><code>.ayjnt/env.d.ts</code> (GeneratedEnv)</li>
			<li><code>.ayjnt/client/&lt;route&gt;/index.tsx</code> (typed useAgent hooks)</li>
			<li><code>.ayjnt/assets/__ayjnt/&lt;route&gt;/{`{index.html, app.js}`}</code> (bundled UIs)</li>
		</ul>
		<p>
			Also updates <code>.ayjnt/migrations.json</code> <em>and writes it
			to disk</em> if the file tree has diverged from the lockfile. This
			is the one command that mutates the committed lockfile —{" "}
			<code>ayjnt dev</code> calls <code>build</code> internally so the
			same happens during dev.
		</p>
		<h3>Exit codes</h3>
		<ul>
			<li><code>0</code> — success.</li>
			<li><code>1</code> — codegen failed (scan found duplicates, parser rejected an agent.ts, etc.).</li>
		</ul>

		<h2>ayjnt migrate</h2>
		<CodeBlock lang="sh" code={`ayjnt migrate`} />
		<p>
			Shows the <em>pending</em> migration — what would be staged on the
			next <code>ayjnt build</code>. Writes nothing. Useful for
			reviewing renames/deletes before you commit.
		</p>
		<CodeBlock
			lang="sh"
			code={`$ bun run migrate
Pending migration: v3 (2026-04-14T12:15:00Z)
  ~ renamed:
      ChatAgent -> TalkAgent (agentId: chat)
  - deleted (storage will be destroyed):
      OldAgent (agentId: old_agent)

Run \`ayjnt build\` to stage this migration in .ayjnt/migrations.json.`}
		/>

		<h2>ayjnt deploy</h2>
		<CodeBlock lang="sh" code={`ayjnt deploy [--force] [wrangler-flags...]`} />
		<p>
			Git preflight → re-build without writing lockfile changes →{" "}
			<code>wrangler deploy</code>. The one command you should only run
			when your working tree is committed and pushed. See{" "}
			<a href="/docs/guides/deployment" class="link-underline">
				Deployment
			</a>{" "}
			for the full walk-through.
		</p>
		<h3>Preflight checks</h3>
		<ol>
			<li><code>git status --porcelain</code> empty</li>
			<li>Local branch not ahead of <code>origin/&lt;branch&gt;</code></li>
			<li>Origin not ahead of local</li>
			<li>No pending migration that hasn't been committed</li>
		</ol>
		<h3>Flags</h3>
		<table>
			<thead>
				<tr>
					<th>Flag</th>
					<th>Effect</th>
				</tr>
			</thead>
			<tbody>
				<tr>
					<td>
						<code>--force</code>
					</td>
					<td>
						Skip all preflight. For emergencies. Loud.
					</td>
				</tr>
				<tr>
					<td>
						<code>--env &lt;name&gt;</code>
					</td>
					<td>
						Pass through to wrangler. Deploys to the named environment
						(<code>staging</code>, <code>production</code>, etc.).
					</td>
				</tr>
				<tr>
					<td>
						<code>--dry-run</code>
					</td>
					<td>
						Pass through to wrangler. Validates the config without
						uploading.
					</td>
				</tr>
			</tbody>
		</table>
		<h3>Exit codes</h3>
		<ul>
			<li><code>0</code> — deployed.</li>
			<li><code>1</code> — preflight failure (ayjnt side).</li>
			<li><em>wrangler's exit code</em> — deploy itself failed.</li>
		</ul>

		<h2>Help</h2>
		<p>
			<code>ayjnt -h</code> or <code>ayjnt --help</code> prints the
			master usage block:
		</p>
		<CodeBlock
			lang="sh"
			code={`ayjnt <command> [options]

Commands:
  new <dir>        Scaffold a new ayjnt project (UI included; --empty for none)
  dev              Start a local development server (wraps wrangler dev)
  build            Generate config + bundle, no deploy
  deploy           Build and deploy to Cloudflare (wraps wrangler deploy)
  migrate          Preview pending migrations from file tree vs lockfile

Global options:
  -h, --help       Show this help
  --cwd <path>     Project root (default: process.cwd())`}
		/>
	</DocPageShell>
</DocsLayout>
